            "review_text": "Sir Andrew Boord Bt.\nIstanbul, Türkiye41 contributions\n0\nSuperb food, warm and friendly atmosphere, marvellous host, great service - what more do you want?\nJul 2017 • Solo\nMy second time in Vietnam and my first in Ho Chi Minh City, Rou was recommended to me by another excellent vegetarian restaurant in Hoi An. I was not disappointed. First, Rou is located centrally but a little out of the somewhat bland swishness of nearby areas in a locality rich in local colour and bustle. From outside the place is modest, but the owner, Quang (please ask for him, he's a superbly warm-hearted, entertaining and informative host) has stamped his personality on the decor - and the menu. I asked for a tasting menu with as much variety as possible and was not disappointed. The curried dish with mushroom - a true fusion masterpiece - was especially memorable, with massive 'meaty' mushrooms bathed in a creamy yet delicate curry sauce. Fresh spring rolls are everywhere in Vietnam and though a personal favourite they can be 'samey'. Not here - just try them out! Quang offered such a variety I wish I had taken notes; in short, great food, a great treat, great value. Give it a try, whether or not you are a vegetarian (which I personally am not!)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 4, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
