            "review_text": "marta110\nEdinburgh, United Kingdom4 contributions\n0\ndirty places full of rats, If you want to catch an infection go there.\nFeb 2017 • Solo\nThat place is close to a hostel I booked (You have to pass the restaurant to reach the hostel) I decided that before going up to the hostel I would eat something in the restaurant that was empty.\nI asked for a vegetarian Indian curry, (59.000dong) on the time they were bringing my food 3 big rats came inside of the restaurant :( believe me I am living in Vietnam for 4 months already and I got use to the rats but not coming inside of a restaurant, coming inside of the kitchen... I was almost to said that I didn´t want the food but they just brought it, I told to the staff and they were laughing of me (very common in vietnamese people).\nWhen I paid the charge VAT 10% and the final bill was 79.000 dong Vietnamise, the food was small and the place full of rats, They just rip me off.\nIt is common sense that if the customer is not satisfied because he saw two rats you can not charge the food vat of a single small dish and scarce.\nWhen I told them they just laugh in my face (very common in Vietnamese people) I felt strongly disagree.\nI worked in hospitaly before and I try to be objective with my critics but honestly you cant eat in a place full of rats and also they will rip you off.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 4, 2017",
